@startuml brightness_call_tree
' Revised 2026-07-12: verified DDC targets and isolated helper transport
!include dark-theme.puml
title Brightness change - full call tree (input sources -> MonitorService -> DDC/VCP)

actor User
participant "GlobalHotkeyService\n(WM_HOTKEY)"      as GHK
participant "App.xaml.cs\n(HandleHotkey / wheel)"   as APP
participant "BrightnessFlyout\n.xaml.cs"            as BFL
participant "EnvironmentalCurveService\n(DispatcherTimer)" as ECS
participant "MonitorInfo\n(model)"                  as MI
participant "MonitorService"                        as MS
participant "AsyncThrottler<string>\nnormal + zero-cooldown immediate" as TH
participant "DDCRecoveryService\n(event-triggered fallback worker;\ncandidates via\nGetStuckRecoveryCandidateIDs)" as DRS
participant "KnownDisplaysStore\n(displays.json)"   as KDS
participant "DisplayService\n(IDisplayService)"     as DS
participant "Per-monitor DDCHelperClient\n+ DDCHelperServer child" as HLP
participant "Dxva2\n(P/Invoke)"                     as DXV
participant "App.RequestTrayRefresh"                as RTR
participant "TrayIconManager"                       as TIM

note over MS
  External monitors use DDC/VCP through dxva2.
  Internal panels can use the Windows WMI brightness transport.
  Both transports enter the same target / verification pipeline.
end note

== Input source 1: slider drag ==
User -> BFL : Slider_PreviewMouseLeftButtonDown\n(track-click branch only)
loop while dragging (or scrubbing master)
  User -> BFL : Slider.ValueChanged TwoWay binding\n-> MonitorInfo.Brightness setter
  BFL -> MI  : Brightness = newVal
  MI  -> BFL : PropertyChanged (gated to integer transitions)
  BFL -> BFL : OnMonitorPropertyChanged\nApplyMasterToEnabledMonitors /\nUpdateMasterFromEnabledIndividuals\n(filter by IsParticipatingInMaster)
  MI  -> MS  : OnMonitorPropertyChanged\n(MonitorService is also subscribed)
  alt _hardwareWritesSuspendCount == 0
    MS -> MS : EnqueueDirectBrightness(monitor, RoundedBrightness)
  else suspended (curve owns hardware on startup restore)
    MS -> MS : skip - slider is pure visual state
  end
  BFL -> RTR : BrightnessUpdated event\n(via EffectiveRoundedBrightness)
  RTR -> TIM : Update(GetBrightnessAndTooltip)\n(UpdateCooldownMs cooldown)
end

== Input source 2: scroll wheel (flyout row or tray icon) ==
User -> BFL : MonitorGrid_PreviewMouseWheel
BFL -> BFL : DisengageCurveForUserAdjustment\n+ AdjustSliderByScrollDelta\n(slider.Value = clamp(...))
note right of BFL
  Tray-icon wheel goes through App.OnTrayWheel:
  for TrayWheelTarget.Brightness it writes
  m.Brightness directly on each monitor
  (same setter -> same MonitorService hook).
end note

== Input source 3: global hotkey ==
User -> GHK : Ctrl+Alt+...\n(WM_HOTKEY on message-only HWND)
GHK -> APP : Fired event (UI thread)
APP -> APP : HandleHotkey(action, parameter)
alt FullBright / FullDim
  APP -> APP : ApplyOrRestoreBrightness(target)\n-> m.Brightness = target
else IncrementMasterBrightness / DecrementMasterBrightness
  APP -> APP : AdjustAllMonitorBrightness(+/-HotkeyStep)\n-> m.Brightness = clamp(m.Brightness + delta)
end
APP -> MI : Brightness = newVal\n(routes through the slider-drag arrows above)
note right of APP
  Hotkey master/all/NL paths (App.xaml.cs:638-657,
  942-978) DO NOT call NotifyUserBrightnessAdjustment
  (distinct from the tray-scroll path which DOES).
  Master is gated out at MonitorService:1580 so master
  itself does not auto-release - but each enabled
  individual it propagates to falls through to the
  OnUserRelease auto-release at :1581 (H-05).
  Individual-row hotkeys: clean disengage via
  OnUserRelease + HarmonizeRow CR-preservation.
end note

== Input source 4: environmental curve evaluator ==
ECS -> ECS : Tick -> Evaluate()\nApplyBrightnessCurve(curve, t, smoothness, absolute)
note right of ECS
  Curve owns hardware; slider thumbs hold user's
  manual intent. Writes BYPASS the Brightness setter
  so the slider thumb does not drag along.
end note
loop for each MonitorInfo where SliderState == CurveActive
  ECS -> MI  : CurveTargetBrightness = absolute or (Brightness + offset)
  ECS -> MS  : EnqueueDirectBrightness(monitor, rowTargetPct)
end

== MonitorService write pipeline (shared by all sources) ==
MS -> MS  : apply norm curve + min/max clamp
MS -> MS  : lock BrightnessTargetGate\ndedupe only pending or read-back-verified pct\nincrement target generation
alt normal input
  MS -> TH : RunAsync(entry.ID, payload)\nlatest-pending-wins + WriteCooldownMs
else mode handoff
  MS -> TH : zero-cooldown RunAsync(entry.ID, payload)\ndrop queued normal payload
end
TH -> MS  : DoBrightnessWriteAsync(entry, target, context)
loop write attempts (ValidationAttempts, ScaledRetryDwellMs)
  MS -> MS  : confirm target generation + ownership predicate\ninside per-monitor DDC lock
  MS -> DS  : TrySetVCPFeature(current DDC snapshot, raw)
  DS -> HLP : stable-identity SETVCP command\ntimeout includes slot + startup + pipe + reply
  HLP -> HLP : enumerate and resolve a fresh DDCMonitor\nopen PHYSICAL_MONITOR[0]
  HLP -> DXV : SetVCPFeature
  DXV --> HLP : ok / Win32 error
  HLP --> DS : OK / FAIL; destroy physical handles
  DS  --> MS
  alt ok
  else transient I2C / monitor busy
    MS -> DS : ResetDDCTransport(monitor)\nretire only this helper process
    MS -> MS : supersession-aware scaled dwell\n<=10 ms response to a newer generation
  end
end

alt write succeeded and target is still current
  MS -> MS : initial commit dwell (max 50 ms)
  MS -> MS : VerifyAppliedAsync(entry, target)
  loop verify attempts (ValidationAttempts)
    MS -> DS  : TryGetVCPFeature(current DDC snapshot)\nunder the same per-monitor lock
    DS -> HLP : stable-identity GETVCP command
    HLP -> HLP : fresh enumerate / resolve / open
    HLP -> DXV : GetVCPFeatureAndVCPFeatureReply
    DXV --> HLP
    HLP --> DS : current + maximum / FAIL
    DS  --> MS
    alt match (within +/- 1 raw unit)
      MS -> MS : complete generation\nLastVerifiedBrightnessPercentage = pct
      MS -> KDS : stamp acknowledged LastBusBrightness
    else readable mismatch
      MS -> MS : RefreshHandle once\npreserve brightness VCP override
      MS -> DS : re-apply current generation\nthen scaled quiet dwell
    else read transport failure
      MS -> DS : ResetDDCTransport(monitor)\nnext GET starts a fresh helper process
      MS -> MS : RefreshHandle once + scaled quiet dwell\nretry GET without another SET
      MS -> MS : supersession-aware scaled dwell
    end
  end
else write retries exhausted while target remains current
  MS -> MS  : DemoteOnDDCFailure(entry, lastWriteError)\nretain immutable recovery identity\n+ invalidate entry target + drop queues
  MS -> DRS : DDCRecoveryRequested(id)\ndirect synchronous wake-up
else target superseded
  MS -> MS : exit without completion or stale re-apply\nnewer generation remains guaranteed to run
end

note over MS
  SetVCPFeature success is transport acceptance, not proof.
  KnownDisplaysStore.LastBusBrightness changes only after
  matching read-back. Canceled/failed targets remain retryable.
  Acquisition no longer hydrates sliders from this value; it reads
  current DDC first, then profile/manual UI state is restored by
  BrightnessFlyout without implicit hardware replay.
end note

note over DS,HLP
  Each helper client belongs to one stable monitor identity.
  MonitorService also calls ResetDDCTransport after a native
  read/write FAIL, not only after timeout / IPC failure. The next
  attempt therefore starts with a fresh process-local dxva2 context.
  Other monitor helpers continue.
end note

== Read paths ==
note over MS
  DDC reads enter through four paths:
   1. Initial/topology probe at MonitorService.Refresh / RefreshProbePhaseAsync
      (immediate on cold start; after the 1500 ms settle for recent topology events).
   2. Verify-after-write via VerifyAppliedAsync.
   3. Refresh re-probe of an existing row.
   4. Targeted fallback via DDCRecoveryService calling TryRecoverMonitor(id).
end note

== DDC fallback acquisition ==
MS -> DRS : DDCRecoveryRequested(id) on demotion\nOR MonitorsRefreshed candidate snapshot
alt failed/read-degraded known-DDC candidates exist
  DRS -> DRS : SignalDDCRecoveryNeeded()\n(single global flag)
  DRS -> DRS : start one worker if idle
  loop immediate first pass, then every 2 seconds while candidates remain
    DRS -> MS : parallel TryRecoverMonitor(id) tasks\nsmall UI snapshot per row only
    MS -> DS : fresh enumeration + remembered identity match\n+ targeted brightness read off dispatcher
    alt acquisition succeeds
      MS -> MS : PromoteRecovered\nclears IsReadDegraded\n+ restores projections
      MS -> ECS : MonitorsRefreshed\nfinal manual/curve ownership reconciliation
      MS -> MS : ReplayRecoveredBrightnessIntent\nforce final owner target through immediate scheduler
      MS -> DS : SET + normal matching read-back\nrecovery GET alone is not application proof
    else acquisition still fails
      MS -> MS : keep Failed / ReadDegraded\nrefresh LastDDCError\ndo not sweep healthy rows
    end
  end
else no candidates
  DRS -> DRS : ClearDDCRecoveryNeeded()\nworker exits
end

note right of DRS
  No per-monitor workers, no MaxRecoveryAttempts terminal state.
  A Failed manual row with a previously verified projected bus value may
  use one best-effort write transport probe, followed immediately by one
  read-back attempt, to distinguish total transport failure from explicit
  unconfirmed compatibility. Once degraded, fallback ticks are read-only
  until reads recover.
end note

note over MS
  Production enforces a positive per-op timeout (minimum 500 ms)
  and includes helper-slot wait, startup, pipe connection, and reply.
  Each stable monitor identity owns an isolated helper process,
  so one hung panel cannot head-of-line block other panels.
  A cumulative deadline across the whole retry pipeline is not modeled.
end note

@enduml
